<title>MEXICO: Mexico says inflation to fall to 7.5 pct by 2000.</title>
<headline>Mexico says inflation to fall to 7.5 pct by 2000.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's inflation rate will drop to 7.5 percent by the year 2000, the government said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Outlining its economic intentions in its National Program for Financing Development 1997-2000, the government gave the following projections:</p>
<p>    YEAR	    YEAR END INFLATION</p>
<p>    1996		    27.7 percent (actual)</p>
<p>    1997		    15.0 percent</p>
<p>    1998		    12.5 percent</p>
<p>    1999		    10.0 percent</p>
<p>    2000		     7.5 percent</p>
<p>((-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
